5,1,1,talk,Minato,,"Hello everyone. I want to make sure the new fee structure is fair, but also that it isn't too hard for the person who has to manage the money. What should we look at first?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,We need a concrete basis for our calculations. I suggest we start by reviewing the last year's ledger of outgoings and the bank statements on last year's renewals to see the actual cash flow.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree with Ryuji on the financial data. However, we should also consider how members actually use the club. I suggest looking at the tally of the sign-in sheets and the sign-up records for mid-year joiners.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,"Numbers are all well and good, but let's not forget the human element. I'm curious about the vibe lately. I'd like to see the weekday turnout since the summer outings and the rota against the attendance record.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we're all eager to dive into the data. While the finances are obvious, I'm more interested in the actual distribution of effort and presence. Let's see who's actually showing up and who's just a name on a list.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minato,,"I see. Everyone has different ideas. I'm worried about the person doing the paperwork, so maybe we should check the outgoing treasurer's logged hours too? It would be good to know how much work it is.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"That is a valid point, Minato. Administrative overhead is a cost in itself. However, we cannot ignore the risk of underfunding. I still believe the bank statements are the most critical piece of evidence for our stability.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Minako,,"It is important to balance the workload with the member experience. If we make the process too rigid or complex to save time, we might discourage people from joining. Let's keep that in mind while we select our data.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, Minako! If we make it feel like a chore or a strict contract, people will hesitate. We want them excited to come, not calculating the cost-benefit ratio every single time they think about joining us.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, calculating the cost-benefit ratio is exactly what people do when they feel they're paying for a service they aren't using—or when they're subsidizing others. Let's be rational about the actual usage patterns.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minato,,"I understand. I just want everyone to be happy and not too stressed. If the work is too much, the treasurer might get sad. Should we also look at the minute books from the named-grade years?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The minute books might provide historical context, but they won't give us the current financial certainty we need. We must prioritize data that reflects our actual current standing to avoid guesswork.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Minako,,"Historical context is useful, but current trends are more pressing. I believe we should focus on the data that shows how newcomers integrate and how often the space is actually used.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, let's not worry about the treasurer's sadness just yet! I'm more concerned about the members' hesitation. I still think the attendance records are key to seeing if people are actually enjoying themselves.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, let's stick to the present. History is fine for a museum, but we're running a club. I'm more interested in the gap between those who do the work and those who just enjoy the perks.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minato,,I think I understand now. I will look into the outgoing treasurer's logged hours and the minute books from the named-grade years. I hope this helps us find a way that is easy for everyone.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will look into the last year's ledger of outgoings and the bank statements on last year's renewals. We must have a clear understanding of our actual balance before we commit to any specific figures.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Minako,,I will look into the sign-up records for mid-year joiners and the tally of the sign-in sheets. I want to see how newcomers are integrating and how the club is being used.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,I'll stick with my gut. I'm going to look into the weekday turnout since the summer outings and the rota against the attendance record. Let's see if people are actually showing up or just hesitating!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll take the rota against the attendance record and the tally of the sign-in sheets. I want a clear picture of who's actually carrying the load and who's just a ghost.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
