30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out that chasing money for individual sessions takes a lot of time—six hours a month! That seems like a lot of work. I think we should avoid any system that makes the treasurer do that.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows that seventy percent of our costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. We cannot afford a system that risks these basics. Furthermore, many members struggle with lump-sum payments, requiring multiple reminders.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The sign-in sheets show a significant gap in attendance, with some members not visiting at all. However, mid-year joiners are hesitant unless we provide custom calculations, which suggests a need for a welcoming, flexible entry process.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,It's exactly as I feared! Turnout dropped after we started charging for outings. People have stopped feeling like these evenings belong to them; they're overthinking it. We've created a psychological barrier that's killing the vibe.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, six hours is a nuisance, but the real issue is the imbalance. A quarter of us are doing two-thirds of the attending, and eighteen people are essentially ghosts. We're subsidizing a lot of empty seats.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I understand, but if the treasurer is too tired from chasing ghosts, they might quit again. Maybe a simple yearly fee is better? It only takes one hour instead of six. That would be much more peaceful.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, a simple yearly fee is efficient, but we must be careful. My findings show that a third of members struggle to pay a lump sum. If we insist on one payment, we risk losing members or increasing the chase.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, if we make the payment structure too rigid, we risk alienating those who can't pay upfront. We need a system that is financially stable but doesn't make members feel scrutinized or excluded.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, a yearly fee sounds peaceful for the treasurer, but it's a huge wall for the members! If we make it a big, scary lump sum, people will hesitate even more before joining. We need to keep it light.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""keeping it light"" is just another way of saying we're ignoring the facts. We have a core group doing all the work and attending everything, while others pay nothing or very little. That's not a vibe; it's an injustice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I don't want anyone to feel it's unfair. But if we make the rules too complicated to be ""just,"" the treasurer has to do all that hard work. Can't we find a way that is both fair and simple?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, simplicity is a goal, but not at the cost of accuracy. We must ensure the fixed costs are covered first. A hybrid approach might be the only rational way to balance stability with accessibility.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, a hybrid approach could work, provided it doesn't create visible tiers of membership. We must ensure that the process for joining remains low-pressure so newcomers don't feel like they are being audited before they even enter.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly! If we start auditing people or creating ""tiers,"" it just adds to that hesitation. We need to make it feel natural to just show up, not like a financial transaction every time.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, making it ""natural"" to show up while a handful of people do all the heavy lifting is exactly how you breed resentment. We can't ignore that eighteen people are ghosts. Rationality requires that those who use the club actually support it.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I hope we can all agree soon. I'm just worried that if we make it too complex to be fair, the treasurer will be too stressed. Let's try to find the simplest way that helps everyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must avoid guesswork. Since seventy percent of our costs are fixed, we need a guaranteed base income, but we must also provide a way to spread payments to avoid the chase. Stability is our priority.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"Stability is necessary, but not at the expense of our culture. If we implement a system that highlights who is a ""ghost"" or who is struggling to pay, we destroy the welcoming atmosphere that makes this club special.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minako, you've hit the nail on the head. If we start treating membership like a subscription service or a debt collection agency, the magic is gone. We need a structure that feels like an invitation, not a bill.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""magic"" doesn't pay the bills or lock the doors. We have nine people doing all the actual work while others treat this place like a free hotel. Let's stop romanticizing the ""vibe"" and start valuing the effort.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
