60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A is the best. It only takes one hour of work for the treasurer, which is much better than six. It's the simplest way and keeps everything peaceful for everyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, while Option A is simple, it ignores the fact that a third of our members struggle with lump sums. Forcing a single payment would likely increase the treasurer's workload through constant chasing.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option B seems too administrative and creates a barrier for every event. Option C is even worse, as it creates visible tiers that would make newcomers feel judged or restricted. I prefer Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, I agree that A is the simplest, but @Ryuji is right about the lump sum. Still, B is a disaster! Charging per event is exactly what killed our weekday turnout. It makes people hesitate.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're prioritizing a ""feeling"" over the fact that a few people are subsidizing the ghosts. Option A is a joke; it rewards the inactive and burdens the loyal. Option C is the only rational way to acknowledge different levels of commitment.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, but Option C sounds complicated. If people have to choose levels, the treasurer has to keep track of who can do what. That sounds like it would take a lot of time and effort.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, you are correct about the complexity. However, Option A is a gamble. If we set a flat fee and people cannot pay it, we lack the funds for our fixed costs. We need a guaranteed baseline.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, we can ensure a baseline with Option A by setting the fee reasonably. Option C would force members to label themselves, which creates a social divide and makes the club feel like a business rather than a community.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly! Labeling people is the worst. If you're a ""Bronze"" member or whatever, you'll feel like a second-class citizen. We need to remove the barriers, not build new ones that make people overthink their value.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, calling it a ""social divide"" is a stretch. It's called accountability. Why should the nine people doing all the work be in the same category as the eighteen ghosts? Option C is the only one that's actually fair.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I don't want anyone to feel it's unfair, but I'm scared that Option C will make the treasurer too tired. If the work is too hard, they might leave, and then we'll have no one to help.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, the treasurer's fatigue is a concern, but financial instability is a greater risk. Option A is too blunt, and Option B is too volatile. Option C provides the most predictable income for our fixed costs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, predictability shouldn't come at the cost of our culture. Option C makes membership a transaction and a label. Option A maintains the anonymity and equality that allows people to drift in and find their feet.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly! We can't let ""predictability"" kill the spirit of the club. If we go with C, people will spend more time worrying about their ""tier"" than actually showing up. Let's just keep it simple and inclusive.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""inclusive"" shouldn't mean ""exploitative."" You're so worried about people overthinking their value that you're ignoring the value provided by the few who actually show up. Option C is the only rational choice for a sustainable club.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I still think Option A is the best. It's the most peaceful for everyone and the easiest for the treasurer. I hope we can choose the simplest way so no one gets too stressed.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, simplicity is not a substitute for stability. Option A risks our fixed costs if payments fail. Option C is the only rational way to secure our baseline while acknowledging actual usage. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I cannot support Option C. It creates a visible hierarchy that would alienate newcomers and destroy the low-pressure environment we need. For the sake of our community's spirit and equality, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm with Minako. Option B is a vibe-killer and C is just a fancy way of labeling people. Let's stop overcomplicating things and just make it easy to belong. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your ""spirit of the club"" is currently being carried on the backs of nine exhausted people. I refuse to support a system that rewards ghosts and penalizes the active. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
